1
00:00:22,799 --> 00:00:26,683
♪The night wind shakes off
the withered leaves♪

2
00:00:29,083 --> 00:00:33,698
♪I open the window and gaze at the moon♪

3
00:00:35,571 --> 00:00:40,709
♪Haze spreads across the river,
lanterns drifting♪

4
00:00:42,047 --> 00:00:47,056
♪I hear the memories rustling♪

5
00:00:48,267 --> 00:00:51,188
♪Garden flowers shed petals one by one♪

6
00:00:51,399 --> 00:00:54,490
♪Candlelight flickers,
swaying with melancholy♪

7
00:00:54,787 --> 00:00:59,022
♪I sigh by the lamp over the long night♪

8
00:01:01,007 --> 00:01:03,915
♪Past memories unfold scene by scene♪

9
00:01:04,213 --> 00:01:07,099
♪It's all your face♪

10
00:01:07,409 --> 00:01:12,191
♪Boldly trampling over my heart♪

11
00:01:12,191 --> 00:01:16,771
♪Two measures of ink I take,
one for love miswritten♪

12
00:01:16,771 --> 00:01:18,770
♪And another for youth passed♪

13
00:01:18,973 --> 00:01:24,755
♪With endless sorrow,
I once traced your silhouette♪

14
00:01:25,139 --> 00:01:29,450
♪Two measures of ink I take,
one for joy and sorrow♪

15
00:01:29,450 --> 00:01:31,958
♪And another for parting and reunion♪

16
00:01:32,204 --> 00:01:42,421
♪I write until splendor fades,
and I am no more♪

17
00:01:45,871 --> 00:01:48,705
=Prelude of the White Snake=

18
00:01:48,705 --> 00:01:51,623
=Episode 11=

19
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:00,640
We're home.

20
00:02:03,879 --> 00:02:04,879
We're home.

21
00:02:07,359 --> 00:02:10,560
How about I walk you to your room?

22
00:02:12,360 --> 00:02:15,080
How about I walk you to your room?

23
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:20,280
You're a lady. I should walk you back.

24
00:02:23,159 --> 00:02:24,599
You've held the umbrella all day.

25
00:02:25,039 --> 00:02:26,039
You must be tired.

26
00:02:26,759 --> 00:02:28,080
Let me walk you back.

27
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:30,960
Holding an umbrella isn't tiring.

28
00:02:35,479 --> 00:02:36,479
Where's the umbrella?

29
00:02:39,719 --> 00:02:40,719
It doesn't matter.

30
00:02:43,599 --> 00:02:44,599
How about

31
00:02:46,360 --> 00:02:47,680
we part here and go back?

32
00:02:51,080 --> 00:02:52,080
Okay.

33
00:03:18,159 --> 00:03:19,159
Are you hungry?

34
00:03:21,520 --> 00:03:22,520
No.

35
00:03:23,599 --> 00:03:25,039
But I'm a bit thirsty.

36
00:03:25,240 --> 00:03:28,639
Aunt's pastry was too salty.

37
00:03:31,360 --> 00:03:32,439
Sorry.

38
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:34,319
How about I get you...

39
00:03:40,719 --> 00:03:42,280
Xu Xian, what's wrong?

40
00:03:43,280 --> 00:03:45,639
I'm fine. You may go back.

41
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:48,800
Xu Xian! Xu...

42
00:03:49,960 --> 00:03:51,560
Xu Xian, what's wrong with you?

43
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:52,840
Xu Xian!

44
00:03:54,560 --> 00:03:56,000
What's wrong with you, Xu Xian?

45
00:03:57,199 --> 00:03:58,199
- Xu Xian!
- I'm fine.

46
00:03:58,199 --> 00:03:59,199
Open the door!

47
00:04:00,120 --> 00:04:01,120
Just go back.

48
00:04:02,120 --> 00:04:03,120
Xu Xian!

49
00:04:04,599 --> 00:04:06,879
Xu Xian, open the door! Xu Xian!

50
00:04:22,160 --> 00:04:23,199
Xu Xian, what's wrong?

51
00:04:28,399 --> 00:04:29,399
(Backlash?)

52
00:04:30,079 --> 00:04:31,680
(How does he have
the Du'e Ancient Scroll?)

53
00:04:32,120 --> 00:04:34,360
(How can a mortal withstand this?)

54
00:04:53,920 --> 00:04:55,759
The Du'e Ancient Scroll
is an ancient artifact.

55
00:04:56,079 --> 00:04:58,240
I can only help you
suppress the backlash temporarily.

56
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:01,600
Xu Xian.

57
00:05:03,600 --> 00:05:04,600
How do you feel?

58
00:05:18,240 --> 00:05:21,959
Just now, dark smoke came out
of the scroll and burrowed into you.

59
00:05:22,600 --> 00:05:24,079
Is it some kind of evil object?

60
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:26,600
No.

61
00:05:26,879 --> 00:05:27,920
It's the Du'e Ancient Scroll.

62
00:05:28,560 --> 00:05:30,720
Master Hanshan passed it on to me.

63
00:05:32,399 --> 00:05:33,839
What is the Du'e Ancient Scroll?

64
00:05:36,800 --> 00:05:39,279
The Du'e Ancient Scroll
is an ancient artifact.

65
00:05:39,759 --> 00:05:41,720
It possesses the purest energies,

66
00:05:42,319 --> 00:05:43,519
and can redeem demons.

67
00:05:44,680 --> 00:05:45,720
Redeem demons?

68
00:05:46,040 --> 00:05:47,040
Using your body?

69
00:05:48,879 --> 00:05:50,959
I just suffer some backlash.

70
00:05:51,959 --> 00:05:53,120
You hate demons the most.

71
00:05:53,399 --> 00:05:54,600
Why would you help them?

72
00:05:59,519 --> 00:06:00,519
Not really.

73
00:06:02,079 --> 00:06:04,000
I only hate the demon
who killed my parents.

74
00:06:05,360 --> 00:06:06,600
Master told me

75
00:06:07,560 --> 00:06:09,319
all beings struggle
on their cultivation,

76
00:06:09,839 --> 00:06:11,439
and they all deserve a second chance.

77
00:06:12,759 --> 00:06:14,519
Some demons are not evil by nature,

78
00:06:15,360 --> 00:06:17,439
and haven't committed terrible crimes.

79
00:06:17,959 --> 00:06:19,160
They've simply lost their way.

80
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:23,160
If someone guides them properly,

81
00:06:23,360 --> 00:06:24,920
they can turn from evil to good,

82
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:26,240
and get on the right path.

83
00:06:30,600 --> 00:06:34,519
Then what about the demon
who killed your parents?

84
00:06:35,040 --> 00:06:36,759
Would you give him a second chance too?

85
00:06:46,480 --> 00:06:47,480
I don't know.

86
00:06:48,360 --> 00:06:49,800
But I would definitely ask him

87
00:06:50,600 --> 00:06:52,399
why he killed my parents.

88
00:07:05,079 --> 00:07:06,079
Why?

89
00:07:06,639 --> 00:07:08,240
- Amitabha.
- Why?

90
00:07:08,240 --> 00:07:09,879
- Why?
- Poor grass.

91
00:07:10,319 --> 00:07:11,839
What did the grass ever do to you?

92
00:07:11,839 --> 00:07:12,959
Cut the nonsense!

93
00:07:13,560 --> 00:07:14,879
Why are you so angry?

94
00:07:15,800 --> 00:07:17,040
You humans are so annoying.

95
00:07:17,879 --> 00:07:19,519
Your lifespans are as short as insects,

96
00:07:20,319 --> 00:07:21,560
yet your desires are endless.

97
00:07:22,279 --> 00:07:24,800
You are also being consumed
by your own desires right now.

98
00:07:25,879 --> 00:07:26,879
Mind your own business.

99
00:07:26,879 --> 00:07:28,120
See? You're ashamed into anger.

100
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:36,720
Can't steady your sword.

101
00:07:37,240 --> 00:07:38,240
So I get it right.

102
00:07:39,040 --> 00:07:40,360
Think I can't deal with you?

103
00:07:41,199 --> 00:07:42,720
The Leifeng Pagoda contract
still stands.

104
00:07:43,240 --> 00:07:44,240
Whenever I want,

105
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:46,639
I can even make you kill yourself.

106
00:07:55,040 --> 00:07:57,000
Pretty.

107
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:58,560
Are you really going to watch me die?

108
00:08:00,160 --> 00:08:01,240
I'm not letting you die.

109
00:08:03,879 --> 00:08:04,879
Thank you.

110
00:08:04,879 --> 00:08:05,879
Thank you.

111
00:08:09,360 --> 00:08:10,360
That scared me.

112
00:08:20,279 --> 00:08:21,680
What's so bad about being a demon?

113
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:25,040
We live longer than humans.

114
00:08:26,759 --> 00:08:28,199
We can travel around

115
00:08:28,759 --> 00:08:29,879
and do whatever we want.

116
00:08:31,560 --> 00:08:32,840
Why must we become an immortal?

117
00:08:34,960 --> 00:08:37,840
Look at those immortals in heaven,
they're all so fake and insincere.

118
00:08:38,279 --> 00:08:39,279
So boring.

119
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:44,600
Love?

120
00:08:47,120 --> 00:08:51,039
Xu Xian's lifespan is shorter than
the time it takes to sober up from a drink.

121
00:08:52,200 --> 00:08:55,000
Yet Suzhen pours her true feelings
into this fleeting romance.

122
00:08:56,519 --> 00:08:57,519
Fool.

123
00:09:00,279 --> 00:09:01,919
This is fate.

124
00:09:03,759 --> 00:09:05,519
All beings have their own fate.

125
00:09:06,759 --> 00:09:07,759
Bai Suzhen has hers.

126
00:09:08,759 --> 00:09:09,759
Xu Xian has his.

127
00:09:10,200 --> 00:09:11,200
So do I.

128
00:09:12,720 --> 00:09:13,720
So do you.

129
00:09:21,960 --> 00:09:24,200
Fahai, let me ask you,

130
00:09:25,360 --> 00:09:27,240
if love is so wonderful,

131
00:09:28,720 --> 00:09:30,080
why is it a trial?

132
00:09:33,360 --> 00:09:34,360
I don't understand.

133
00:09:40,840 --> 00:09:42,440
Love is born from desire.

134
00:09:43,600 --> 00:09:46,679
Desire arises from craving,

135
00:09:48,440 --> 00:09:49,879
and the trial begins.

136
00:09:51,960 --> 00:09:53,000
Then I'll crave too.

137
00:09:54,440 --> 00:09:56,000
I want to be with Suzhen forever.

138
00:09:58,960 --> 00:10:00,320
Is this my trial?

139
00:10:08,320 --> 00:10:10,200
Look at this half-snake,
half-drake freak.

140
00:10:10,639 --> 00:10:12,080
An unnatural monster.

141
00:10:12,639 --> 00:10:13,639
Strip it bare

142
00:10:13,679 --> 00:10:14,799
to check its gender.

143
00:10:20,679 --> 00:10:21,679
You lesser demons!

144
00:10:21,679 --> 00:10:23,480
How dare you pick on the weak

145
00:10:23,480 --> 00:10:24,480
in here?

146
00:10:24,960 --> 00:10:26,240
Do you want to revert

147
00:10:26,240 --> 00:10:27,240
to your original forms?

148
00:10:27,600 --> 00:10:28,600
Miss Bai, sorry.

149
00:10:28,720 --> 00:10:30,159
We won't dare to do it again.

150
00:10:30,480 --> 00:10:31,480
Get lost now!

151
00:10:46,759 --> 00:10:48,240
So you're that mixed-blood demon?

152
00:10:49,879 --> 00:10:52,279
I've never seen
a little snake with horns before.

153
00:10:52,600 --> 00:10:53,799
So adorable.

154
00:10:56,120 --> 00:10:57,440
You're so beautiful.

155
00:10:57,639 --> 00:10:59,759
Don't you think I'm weird and ugly?

156
00:11:00,799 --> 00:11:02,159
How could you be ugly?

157
00:11:03,039 --> 00:11:05,519
You're the most adorable snake
I've ever seen.

158
00:11:06,120 --> 00:11:07,639
I'll take you as my younger sister.

159
00:11:08,600 --> 00:11:09,679
What do you think?

160
00:11:12,559 --> 00:11:13,879
I'm used to being alone,

161
00:11:14,360 --> 00:11:15,360
but you're cute enough

162
00:11:15,600 --> 00:11:16,600
for me to make an exception.

163
00:11:17,200 --> 00:11:20,399
From now on, you'll be
the only important person by my side.

164
00:11:22,200 --> 00:11:23,200
Alright?

165
00:11:27,039 --> 00:11:28,639
You said I'm the only one.

166
00:11:32,200 --> 00:11:34,840
I know you won't
get over this right away.

167
00:11:36,039 --> 00:11:37,519
Why don't you just wait and see?

168
00:11:37,720 --> 00:11:39,440
See if Bai Suzhen abandons you

169
00:11:39,879 --> 00:11:41,120
when Xu Xian's with her.

170
00:11:45,480 --> 00:11:46,480
Be quiet?

171
00:11:47,399 --> 00:11:48,799
Then it's settled.

172
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:50,919
Change back into men's clothes.

173
00:11:50,919 --> 00:11:52,639
Let's go to Cuiyu Pavilion
and have a drink.

174
00:11:52,720 --> 00:11:53,720
I promise you,

175
00:11:53,720 --> 00:11:55,360
we won't go home until we're drunk.

176
00:11:57,039 --> 00:11:59,240
No. You'll go drink by yourself.

177
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:03,600
Wait for me.

178
00:12:16,399 --> 00:12:17,399
- Come on.
- Come on.

179
00:12:17,600 --> 00:12:18,600
Cheers.

180
00:12:35,840 --> 00:12:37,080
How did I lose again?

181
00:12:38,679 --> 00:12:40,639
Did you secretly use spells?

182
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:43,559
If you can't afford to lose, don't play.

183
00:12:45,320 --> 00:12:46,320
Seriously.

184
00:12:46,639 --> 00:12:48,320
The contract with you

185
00:12:48,320 --> 00:12:49,440
is affecting my luck.

186
00:12:56,799 --> 00:12:57,799
Pretty,

187
00:12:58,799 --> 00:13:02,240
how about you
just release me from it first?

188
00:13:02,480 --> 00:13:04,799
After you do, we can play another round,

189
00:13:05,440 --> 00:13:07,279
and I definitely won't lose.

190
00:13:16,639 --> 00:13:18,559
Forget about your little schemes.

191
00:13:19,759 --> 00:13:21,240
I'm not drunk.

192
00:13:27,399 --> 00:13:28,480
Another round.

193
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:49,559
Come on, cheers.

194
00:13:49,559 --> 00:13:50,559
Cheers.

195
00:14:09,480 --> 00:14:10,480
Qing?

196
00:14:12,279 --> 00:14:13,559
How did you get so drunk?

197
00:14:14,039 --> 00:14:15,200
You're Miss Bai's bodyguard.

198
00:14:15,679 --> 00:14:16,679
If she's in danger,

199
00:14:16,679 --> 00:14:17,679
how will you protect her?

200
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:20,440
Bodyguard?

201
00:14:23,399 --> 00:14:24,639
You are here.

202
00:14:28,799 --> 00:14:30,799
You're drunk. I'll take you home.

203
00:14:32,919 --> 00:14:34,039
I'm not drunk.

204
00:14:35,519 --> 00:14:37,639
My mind is clear, perfectly clear.

205
00:14:39,679 --> 00:14:41,279
Suzhen likes you so much,

206
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:45,960
As a grown man,
why are you being so hesitant?

207
00:14:47,759 --> 00:14:51,799
I've been through thick and thin
with Suzhen for so many years.

208
00:14:53,399 --> 00:14:55,559
Who do you think you are?

209
00:14:58,080 --> 00:14:59,440
I understand her better.

210
00:15:00,919 --> 00:15:01,919
I care about her more.

211
00:15:03,879 --> 00:15:05,480
But now, because of you,

212
00:15:08,480 --> 00:15:10,480
she's about to abandon me.

213
00:15:13,679 --> 00:15:15,799
Qing, you really are drunk.

214
00:15:16,440 --> 00:15:17,720
I'm not drunk.

215
00:15:18,039 --> 00:15:19,559
Listen carefully.

216
00:15:21,320 --> 00:15:23,679
You must treat Suzhen well.

217
00:15:28,639 --> 00:15:29,960
If you dare to betray her,

218
00:15:30,399 --> 00:15:32,080
I won't let you off.

219
00:15:35,639 --> 00:15:37,279
I will definitely

220
00:15:38,639 --> 00:15:41,639
rip your tendons out,
skin you, and cut you to pieces.

221
00:15:43,039 --> 00:15:44,039
Qing.

222
00:15:46,559 --> 00:15:47,559
You...

223
00:15:49,279 --> 00:15:50,279
- Qing.
- Suzhen.

224
00:15:50,279 --> 00:15:51,480
What's wrong, Qing?

225
00:15:53,080 --> 00:15:54,080
Suzhen.

226
00:15:58,759 --> 00:16:01,360
Do you like Xu Xian,

227
00:16:03,039 --> 00:16:04,759
and not like me anymore?

228
00:16:08,320 --> 00:16:09,320
Young Master Xu.

229
00:16:09,440 --> 00:16:10,440
You two should go.

230
00:16:10,600 --> 00:16:14,360
Xu Xian, just let me explain.

231
00:16:17,720 --> 00:16:20,799
Qing, you've messed things up.

232
00:16:52,964 --> 00:16:57,123
♪I also gave my youth to someone♪

233
00:16:59,590 --> 00:17:03,968
♪I must admit, you made the journey♪

234
00:17:05,511 --> 00:17:11,336
♪When loving you
became instinct, what's left♪

235
00:17:12,105 --> 00:17:16,572
♪Seals a fate too brutal to amend♪

236
00:17:19,437 --> 00:17:23,878
♪Clumsy and new, we gave our first kiss♪

237
00:17:26,074 --> 00:17:30,804
♪Never thought passionate eyes
would turn cold♪

238
00:17:32,016 --> 00:17:38,129
♪I thought of pulling away,
but I'd barely begun♪

239
00:17:38,792 --> 00:17:44,574
♪Having loved you so deep,
how could I love another♪

240
00:17:44,574 --> 00:17:50,837
♪Even if we're strangers again,
why deny we loved♪

241
00:17:51,147 --> 00:17:57,506
♪Though I'm stubborn,
I never stopped you from loving others♪

242
00:17:57,677 --> 00:18:05,044
♪I shouldn't have been so foolish
to think there was still hope♪

243
00:18:05,329 --> 00:18:10,876
♪But you won't even admit what we had♪

244
00:18:11,367 --> 00:18:17,577
♪Even if we're strangers again,
why deny we loved♪

245
00:18:17,887 --> 00:18:24,660
♪Though I have questions,
I never questioned you♪

246
00:18:25,657 --> 00:18:31,310
♪I'll lock you away and set myself free♪

247
00:18:32,144 --> 00:18:36,552
♪After all, I'm the one you deny♪

248
00:18:37,317 --> 00:18:39,905
♪Having ever loved♪
